# Ockham's lean tree (2026-11-08): what default code search skips.
#
# This file changes nothing in Git: every path below stays tracked, pinned and
# checked out exactly as before. It is read by ripgrep and tools built on it
# (Claude Code's Grep, Codex and other agents' `rg`, VS Code search), so a
# repository-wide search returns code and notes instead of ~97% job outputs,
# data, attempt receipts, scans and frozen work papers. Search one of these on
# purpose by naming it (`rg term jobs/claim-kit/output`, or Grep with that path)
# or with `rg -uu`. See .claude/hooks/ockham_lean_tree.py for the listing guard.

jobs/*/output/
jobs/*/data/
jobs/*/work/
jobs/_attempts/
/research/excavator/
/research/production/
/research/stage*/
/research/releases/
/ProQuest Pre-1937 Orders/
/releases/
/*.part0?
/oversized/
/.job-cache/
